Lunacy's Device Info.

Palm's own Device Info (com.palm.app.deviceinfo, webOS 3.x) reports a webOS device: its
Palm profile, its webOS version, its carrier and its hardware. Lunacy is not a webOS device
and doesn't own most of what that app reports, so this app is written for Lunacy: it reports
the environment the apps actually run in, and hands settings that belong to Android to
Android. It keeps Palm's app id, so it sits where webOS users expect to find it, and Palm's
icons, so it looks like it belongs.

The app's code is Lunacy's, under the same terms as the rest of Lunacy. These files are not:

- icon.png, icon-256x256.png, images/header-icon-deviceinfo.png

  Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard, from com.palm.app.deviceinfo as shipped on webOS
  3.x. Never released under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like
  Mojo and the Prelude fonts (no owner has asserted rights since webOS was discontinued).
